WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:06.950
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and since the
Time Lords are trying to come back into the

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:11.370
regular Universe I wanted to float the theory
that we’ll see other Time Lords in Series

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.919
8, Series 9 or some point in the future.

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:15.660
This opens the door for people that may not
necessarily make good Doctor’s, but would

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.070
make excellent Time Lords.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.539
Just remember of all the voices from The Doctor’s
Wife.

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:22.720
I’ll also be doing a video for my top 10
choices for a new companion next week.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:29.090
Be sure to subscribe to get it and leave suggestions
in the comments.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.480
One of the beauties of all this is that new
Time Lords can be quick cameos, opening the

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.660
door to some of our more favorite actors that
are too busy to play The Doctor himself.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.350
Cue the fan fiction!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.620
Number 10 - Andrew Scott.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:45.530
He’s been the quintessential villain since
Sherlock Series 1 but his portrayal of Moriarty

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:49.320
has this playfulness that feels just like
a madman in a box.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.360
There have even been some Sherlock actors
that guested during Matt Smith’s run like

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.570
Rupert Graves.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.010
As much fun as it would be to see him become
Doctor Who’s greatest nemesis The Master,

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.490
I feel like that would too obvious of a choice.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.780
So giving Scott the opportunity to channel
his crazy performance into a good character

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.790
would be a nice change of pace.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.750
And he’d still have all of Time and Space
with which to cause mischief.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.049
Number 9 - Tom Hardy as The Warrior.

00:01:11.049 --> 00:01:15.719
The existence of the War Doctor is proof that
Time Lords can be Warriors.

00:01:15.719 --> 00:01:19.840
So wouldn’t it be fun to see the very large
physically imposing Tom Hardy play a Time

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.760
Lord that was still in a warrior incarnation
of himself.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.340
Just because you’re a warrior doesn’t
mean you have to be a villain.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.399
The Doctor’s code, Never Cruel or Cowardly
is something unique to him.

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:32.799
Not all Time Lords have to have laid down
their swords after the Time War ended.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:36.939
I’d really like to see Peter Capaldi meet
another Warrior Time Lord and try to get him

00:01:36.939 --> 00:01:37.939
to chill.

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:42.020
Or he could just be a big fun buiser like
Christopher Eccleston’s Doctor.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.259
Number 8 - Jude Law.

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:44.740
The Pretty Boy Time Lord.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.070
I’m just joking with the pretty boy, but
for a lot of his career that’s what Jude

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:49.950
Law was known as.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:54.039
I think he’d do an amazing job of playing
a post-gender swapped Time Lord.

00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:58.049
During Doctor’s Wife Matt Smith even alluded
to the fact he had a relationship with another

00:01:58.049 --> 00:02:00.139
Time Lord that went from female to male.

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:02.390
Jude Law could totally play that character
or one like him.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.010
Father kind of implied in that episode that
all of the gallifreyan message cubes belonged

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.999
to Time Lords he had killed.

00:02:06.999 --> 00:02:09.430
Number 7 - Ralph Fiennes as a new Rassilon.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:13.580
Timothy Dalton was amazing as Rassilon during
Russel T. Davies run, but because the tone

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.030
of the show has changed so much since the
10th Doctor and will continue to get darker.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:22.420
I think Lord Voldemort would bring the right
level of intensity to the ruler of the Time

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:23.420
Lords.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.720
There have been a lot of theories about where
Rassilon was during the events of the 50th

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.720
Anniversary.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.470
And confusion over whether or not he’s still
trapped in that Time Locked bubble from End

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:31.470
of Time.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.130
But for the purposes of this video, let’s
assume he’s on Gallifrey with all the other

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.520
citizens right now.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.000
Vote Yes For Lord Voldemort Rassilon!

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.830
Number 6 - Dame Helen Mirren as The Woman
in White.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:44.960
So many theories about her being the Doctor’s
mother, but let’s assume that she’s not

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:48.310
so we can open the doors on making her a good
foil for River Song.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.220
Also rumored to return.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.730
Who would ever be able to out-River Song River
Song but The Queen of England.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.640
She’s such an amazing actress she could
play any of the major characters on the show

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.340
like a Female Master, making her The new Woman
in White would just be a good pairing for

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:05.950
an episode or future anniversary special that
featured my Rassilon dream-pick Ralph Fiennes.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:10.190
Not that you have to feature both characters
in the same story, it’s just that the last

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.150
time we saw them they were in close proximity.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.590
Number 5 - Gwendoline Christie as Romana.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:19.010
Pre-50th Anniversary her status was alive
slash unknown.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.120
In some of the non-tv series material she
even took Rassilon’s job as President for

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.120
a brief period.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.230
Regardless of the previous portrayals of the
character.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:29.960
As Brienne on Game of Thrones Gwendoline is
one of the most positive and powerful women

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.580
in Science Fiction and Fantasy, super powers
notwithstanding.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:37.580
The Woman in White is another powerful female
Time Lord, but I always viewed that character

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.320
being played by an older actress.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:43.210
Romana on the other hand seems like it would
be a better choice for someone younger.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:46.890
Gwendolyne would be about 3 inches taller
than Capaldi, so it would make for some great

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.320
visual gags too.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.760
As in you may be a mentor to me, but I am
probably going to be the one to pull your

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.850
ass out the Time Fire.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.470
Number 4 - Hugh Laurie as The Meddling Monk.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:00.070
Think Blackadder, Jeeves and Wooster Hugh
Laurie, not House Hugh Laurie.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.250
We spent so much time watching him playing
a character that resembled the War Doctor.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:07.760
It would be so much fun to watch Laurie go
back to his comedy roots and play a Loki-type

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:08.760
Time Lord.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.210
He’s not evil, he just likes to make a mess
of things.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:14.090
Who better to clean them up than the stern
12th Doctor.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.060
Just picture Capaldi giving Laurie the stare.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.009
Number 3 - Ben Whishaw as The Scholar.

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:23.469
I don’t really see him playing the same
type of Time Lord as a hulking Tom Hardy,

00:04:23.469 --> 00:04:28.030
but Ben Whishaw was one of my top picks for
the 12th Doctor before Peter Capaldi was announced.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:31.530
Imagine an amalgam of his characters from
James Bond and The Hollow Crown.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:35.300
I’d really like to see him as a bookish
Time Lord who Capaldi would go to for assistance

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.430
with an unsolvable riddle.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:42.550
Picture his TARDIS looking like a more grand
version of the one we saw in Series 7.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.039
Number 2 - Tom Hiddleston.

00:04:44.039 --> 00:04:47.270
Starting to break into the realm of fan fiction
but this is a wish list.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.320
He even co-starred with Whishaw in The Hollow
Crown.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:54.940
He’s been the consummate bad guy since Thor
but I think he has the perfect level of ambiguity

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.400
that would be perfect for a Time Lord.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:01.939
The Doctor always said that the Time War twisted
his people, Imagine the scene in Avengers

00:05:01.939 --> 00:05:06.150
where Loki steps out of the portal for the
first time looking haunted and derranged.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.900
But not totally evil.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.400
Imagine a Time Lord burdened with glorious
purpose.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.990
Mewling Quims for the win.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.639
and my number 1 pick for a new Time Lord.

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:15.740
Chiwetel Ejiofor.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.070
The rumored almost-12th Doctor.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:22.400
Chiwetel was supposedly the anglo-african
actor offered the role of The Doctor but then

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.490
turned it down.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.650
This is all based on conjecture from a statement
Neil Gaiman made.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.169
But it’s since passed into fan fic legend.

00:05:30.169 --> 00:05:34.090
If he was good enough to play the Doctor and
he’s probably going to win a Best Actor

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:37.330
Oscar, just think of what he would bring to
a Time Lord character.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:44.069
So there’s a lot of amazing actors like
Idris Elba, Eddie Redmayne, Aiden Turner and

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:45.330
Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:48.330
But we have to set aside a few for potential
choices for a new “Master”.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:51.629
If there’s anything I really want to see
from Series 8 and Capaldi’s run it’s a

00:05:51.629 --> 00:05:52.840
new major Time Lord character.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.979
Not one that we see all the time.

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:58.330
Just someone really important like Rassilon
or even River Song.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.569
Based on a lot of comments from the production
staff everyone thinks we’ll be seeing a

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:05.150
lot of Classic Who bits returning but I also
really hope Moffat introduces something big

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.379
and new into the Canon.

00:06:06.379 --> 00:06:10.220
Now it’s your turn, let me know which actors
you’d love to see play a Time Lord in Series

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:11.400
8 or 9.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.370
Think young actors and old.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.740
They can even play pre-existing characters.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:19.509
Unless we get some big surprise news from
the set, my next Doctor Who video will be

00:06:19.509 --> 00:06:25.349
10 picks for a new companion either in addition
to or in replacement of Jenna Louise Coleman.

00:06:25.349 --> 00:06:26.419
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:30.770
We don’t know if she’s going to stay on
for series 9 yet.

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:35.320
Right now click here to learn more about Series
8 and click here for my Sherlock Series 4

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.320
Predictions.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.490
Thanks for watching, see you tomorrow.

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:38.029
High Fives!

